{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Image Generation \u2014 GANs Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Generator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A small DCGAN generator that takes 64-dim noise and produces a 32x32 image."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Generator(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, z_dim=64, img_channels=3, feat=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.net = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ConvTranspose2d(z_dim, feat * 4, kernel_size=4, stride=1, padding=0, bias=False),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.BatchNorm2d(feat * 4),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ConvTranspose2d(feat * 4, feat * 2, kernel_size=4, stride=2, padding=1, bias=False),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.BatchNorm2d(feat * 2),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ConvTranspose2d(feat * 2, feat, kernel_size=4, stride=2, padding=1, bias=False),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.BatchNorm2d(feat),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ConvTranspose2d(feat, img_channels, kernel_size=4, stride=2, padding=1, bias=False),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Tanh(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, z):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.net(z.view(z.size(0), -1, 1, 1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Four transposed convs, each with `kernel_size=4, stride=2, padding=1` so they cleanly double spatial size. Output activations in [-1, 1] via tanh."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Discriminator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Mirror of the generator. LeakyReLU, strided convs, ends with a scalar logit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Discriminator(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, img_channels=3, feat=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.net = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(img_channels, feat, kernel_size=4, stride=2, padding=1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.LeakyReLU(0.2, inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(feat, feat * 2, kernel_size=4, stride=2, padding=1, bias=False),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.BatchNorm2d(feat * 2),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.LeakyReLU(0.2, inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(feat * 2, feat * 4, kernel_size=4, stride=2, padding=1, bias=False),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.BatchNorm2d(feat * 4),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.LeakyReLU(0.2, inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(feat * 4, 1, kernel_size=4, stride=1, padding=0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.net(x).view(-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The last conv reduces a `4x4` feature map to `1x1`. Output is a single scalar per image; apply sigmoid only during loss computation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Training step"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Alternate: update D once, then G once, every batch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_step(G, D, real, z, opt_g, opt_d, device):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    real = real.to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bs = real.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # D step"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    opt_d.zero_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    d_real = D(real)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    d_fake = D(G(z).detach())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss_d = (F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(d_real, torch.ones_like(d_real))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "              + F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(d_fake, torch.zeros_like(d_fake)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss_d.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    opt_d.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # G step"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    opt_g.zero_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    d_fake = D(G(z))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss_g = F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(d_fake, torch.ones_like(d_fake))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss_g.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    opt_g.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return loss_d.item(), loss_g.item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`G(z).detach()` in the D step is critical: we do not want gradients flowing into G during its update. Forgetting that is the classic beginner bug."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Full training loop on synthetic shapes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, TensorDataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def synthetic_images(num=2000, size=32, seed=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    imgs = np.zeros((num, 3, size, size), dtype=np.float32) - 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(num):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        r = rng.uniform(6, 12)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        cx, cy = rng.uniform(r, size - r, size=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        yy, xx = np.meshgrid(np.arange(size), np.arange(size), indexing=\"ij\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mask = (xx - cx) ** 2 + (yy - cy) ** 2 < r ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        color = rng.uniform(-0.5, 1.0, size=3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for c in range(3):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            imgs[i, c][mask] = color[c]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return torch.from_numpy(imgs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "device = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "data = synthetic_images()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "loader = DataLoader(TensorDataset(data), batch_size=64, shuffle=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "G = Generator(z_dim=64, img_channels=3, feat=32).to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "D = Discriminator(img_channels=3, feat=32).to(device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "opt_g = torch.optim.Adam(G.parameters(), lr=2e-4, betas=(0.5, 0.999))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "opt_d = torch.optim.Adam(D.parameters(), lr=2e-4, betas=(0.5, 0.999))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for epoch in range(10):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for (batch,) in loader:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        z = torch.randn(batch.size(0), 64, device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ld, lg = train_step(G, D, batch, z, opt_g, opt_d, device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"epoch {epoch}  D {ld:.3f}  G {lg:.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`Adam(lr=2e-4, betas=(0.5, 0.999))` is the DCGAN default \u2014 the low beta1 keeps the momentum term from stabilising the adversarial game too much."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Sampling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@torch.no_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sample(G, n=16, z_dim=64, device=\"cpu\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    G.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    z = torch.randn(n, z_dim, device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    imgs = G(z)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    imgs = (imgs + 1) / 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return imgs.clamp(0, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Always switch to eval mode before sampling. For DCGAN this matters because batch norm running stats are used instead of the batch's stats."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Spectral normalisation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A drop-in replacement for BN in the discriminator that guarantees the network is 1-Lipschitz. Fixes most \"D wins too hard\" failures."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torch.nn.utils import spectral_norm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def build_sn_discriminator(img_channels=3, feat=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        spectral_norm(nn.Conv2d(img_channels, feat, 4, 2, 1)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        nn.LeakyReLU(0.2, inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        spectral_norm(nn.Conv2d(feat, feat * 2, 4, 2, 1)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        nn.LeakyReLU(0.2, inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        spectral_norm(nn.Conv2d(feat * 2, feat * 4, 4, 2, 1)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        nn.LeakyReLU(0.2, inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        spectral_norm(nn.Conv2d(feat * 4, 1, 4, 1, 0)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Swap `Discriminator` for `build_sn_discriminator()` and you often do not need the TTUR trick. Spectral norm is the easiest single robustness upgrade you can apply."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Train the DCGAN above on the synthetic circle dataset and save a grid of 16 samples at the end of each epoch. By which epoch do the generated circles become clearly circular?\n2. **(Medium)** Replace the discriminator's batch norm with spectral norm. Train both versions side by side. Which one converges faster? Which one has lower variance across three seeds?\n3. **(Hard)** Implement a conditional DCGAN: feed the class label into both G and D (concat one-hot to the noise in G, concat a class embedding channel in D). Train on the synthetic \"circles vs squares\" dataset from lesson 7 and show that class conditioning works by sampling with specific labels."
      ]
    }
  ],
